SupraLINUX kquickcharts packaging notes

Authority is KDE Frameworks upstream stable 6.30.0. Ubuntu 26.04 Resolute is a provider platform only. Debian 6.28 packaging is retained only as a technical baseline for Debian-family binary names, package splits and symbols metadata.

The active .symbols files are not stored in this package tree. The Batch 10 runner materializes the hash-pinned Debian 6.28 references into the ephemeral source package and validates architecture-aware required export floors before accepting PASS.

QCH follows the common SupraLINUX Frameworks profile and is disabled. Upstream tests remain enabled. No downstream test-suppression patch or behavior patch is retained.

debian/copyright.reference is provenance metadata only. The package runner materializes the complete hash-pinned Debian 6.28 copyright file from retained artifact 10301938362 into the ephemeral source package; SupraLINUX does not keep a second mutable copy in git.

Attempt-1 ABI remediation
-------------------------

The first real KQuickCharts package attempt ran only after the current-run SupraLINUX Kirigami 6.30.0-0supralinux2 PASS artifact satisfied the QML/runtime package-validation predecessor. The KQuickCharts build then passed 8/8 upstream tests but dpkg-gensymbols rejected two retained Debian 6.28 std::_Sp_counted_ptr<QQuickItem *> RTTI/vtable exports that are absent with the current Resolute toolchain.

These exports are C++ standard-library template-instantiation implementation details, not public KQuickCharts API. Revision 6.30.0-0supralinux2 applies a deterministic hash-guarded overlay immediately before dh_makeshlibs and changes only those two lines from arch=!riscv64 to optional=templinst|arch=!riscv64. Their historical 6.0.0 minimum is preserved. The already-optional std::_Rb_tree::find template symbol is deliberately unchanged.

